        <p>for both crown and brim, the former having a faint resemblance to a Tam-o'Shanter in shape, and the brim being pleated all round and edged with an inch-wide strapping of black silk. On either side of the front comes an enormous "market" bunch of little crimson-rambler roses, edged all round with their pretty, green foliage. From the bunch on the left spring two big soft quills, with black centres and white edges.</p>
