        <head>LTIIE END. 1</head>
        <p>LTIIE END. 1</p>
        <p>PENKETH AND SANKEY.</p>
        <p>ST. MARY'S CHURCH (SANKEY.)—A handsome memorial window was unveiled in the above Church on Sunday morning. It has been erected in the north wall, and is the gift of Mr. Edward Dignum, of Toronto, to the memory of his father and mother, John and Ellen Hatton Dignum. The window, which was designed by Messrs. Jones and Willis, consists of three ranels, illustrative of three scenes in the life of St. Paul. It was unveiled by Mr. J. B. Aitken, who paid a warm tribute to his old friend in the following words : —" The Vicar having asked me to take a part in to-day's proceedings, in respect to the dedication of the memorial window which Mr. Edward Dignum has</p>
