        <p>juryman is in a fit condition to appreciate the evidence in the case. That being so I shall adjourn the inquiry until Wednesday. After consultation witlais clerk the Coroner decided not to adjourn, but to swear-in a policeman as juryman in order that the inquiry might be finished. The juror was then taken from the room by another constable who took him into custody. The Coroner afterwards proceeded with the inquiry. He remarked that it would be far better if the company had a bridge of their own in a place where it would tempt people to go over the line instead of by the level crossing. The jury returned a verdict of " Accidental Death," end added suggestions that a new bridge should be made and a booking office provided on each side of the 4a Um</p>
