        <p>INSTANT RELIEF RAPID CURE of GOUT AND RHEUMATISM by EA.DE'S PILLS. THE SWELLING DISAPPEARED ! ! H.M.S. Leander, Davenport, November 30th, 1907. Dear Sir.—During the past six months we have had some extremely damp and foggy weather, and whilst hoisting in and out ocean tugs, copper punts and other small crafts I contracted several chills one after the other, which finally settled in my legs and and feet, causing them to swell ; and to make matters worse I had the misfortune to fall out of a submerged;torpedo tube,and sprained both ankles. I was placed on the sick list and given the usual naval treatment, which did me no good. Seeing your advertisement, I determined to try your famous Gout:Pills, and after taking a few doses they worked marvels. All the swelling disappeared and my legs are as strong as ever again. Yours Respectfully, G. SWACKENTIAMMEIt. Q.G. EADE'S GOUT PILLS Are perfectly safe in their action, eliminate all jurilus matter, and are highly restorative old everywhere in Bottles, is lid and 2 9d, or sent post free for stamps or P.O. by the Porprietors, GEORGE EADE, 232, Goswell road London. IEUMATIC PILLS.</p>
        <p>Marriages. BELK—BURTON.—On the 23rd inst.at the Congregational Chapel. Chapel-street, Southport, Henry Francis, onlY son of the late W. Belk Esq. of Hartlepool, to - Minnie, third daughter of T. Burton Esq., of Warrington. , LIALLAWAY—GERRARD—At St. Cuthbert's Church, Carlisle, on the 29th ult., by the Rev. Canon Bower, assisted by the Rev. Nigel F. Stone, Augustus Thornburn Hallaway, to Frances Devell Gerrard, of LTulev Park, Adelaide, Australia. BUCKLEY—Wncocrcs—April 28th, at the Parish Church, Warrington by the Rev. Canon Willis, John. Henry Buckley to Annie Wilcocks. EVANS—GIBSON—ApriI 28th, at , the Parish Church, Warrington, by the Rev. T. W. Barber, George Smith Evans to Helena Gibson. ELLISON—ASTILL—ApriI 29th, at the Parish Churcbr Warrington, by the Rev. Canon Willis, Luke Ellisoa to Florence Astill.</p>
